      "side": 1,
      "message": "This forces `mRecordingContext.needsSubmit` true so [this](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/QueueVk.cpp;l\u003d322-324;drc\u003dc5c93224f7412a71a58c7951977ca798413e1bcf) doesn\u0027t skip the submit. That is kind of hacky of course.\n\nOne other potential solution is to keep using `GetPendingCommandSerial()` as the serial for FencedDeleter to delete at. Here we can check if `mRecordingContext.used` and `mRecordingContext.needsSubmit` are both false then advance the submitted and completed serial without doing a submit. Otherwise if there is work this code can run `queue-\u003eForceEventualFlushOfCommands()` and wait for the submit/work to finish.",
